From: skyjet18 <57456827+skyjet18@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 08:25:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 40/49] [FFmpeg-devel,1/2] avformat hls fix to seek logic

https://patchwork.ffmpeg.org/project/ffmpeg/patch/20200424152042.29383-2-hello.vectronic@gmail.com/

Ported to FFmpeg 9.0.2 from 0008-FFmpeg-devel-1-2-avformat-hls-fix-to-seek-logic.patch.
The keyframe condition in hls_read_packet() is applied as in the
original. The comment change in hls_read_seek() is already upstream
("mpegts/mov demuxer"). 9.0.2 also moves backward video seeks to the
segment start in hls_read_seek(); that is kept.
---
 libavformat/hls.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
index 6b3e7673..0d6e0a1d 100644
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -2810,8 +2810,10 @@ static int hls_read_packet(AVFormatContext *s, AVPacket *pkt)
                     ts_diff = av_rescale_rnd(pls->pkt->dts, AV_TIME_BASE,
                                             tb.den, AV_ROUND_DOWN) -
                             pls->seek_timestamp;
-                    if (ts_diff >= 0 && (pls->seek_flags  & AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY ||
-                                        pls->pkt->flags & AV_PKT_FLAG_KEY)) {
+                    /* If AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY, keep reading until ts_diff is greater than 0
+                     * otherwise return the first keyframe encountered */
+                    if ((ts_diff >= 0 && (pls->seek_flags & AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY)) ||
+                        (!(pls->seek_flags & AVSEEK_FLAG_ANY) && (pls->pkt->flags & AV_PKT_FLAG_KEY)))  {
                         pls->seek_timestamp = AV_NOPTS_VALUE;
                         break;
                     }
